Confirmed: `smokeSettings.Environment` = config `smoke.environment` (default PATH,HOME,TMPDIR,LANG,LC_ALL). And `smokeEnvironment` in smoke_protocol.go:623-642 forwards ALL of settings.Environment unconditionally — the manifest.Environment list only appends names already in the settings allowlist (a no-op given `names` starts as a copy of settings.Environment).

Wait, let me re-read carefully:

```go
func smokeEnvironment(settings SmokeSettings, manifest smokeManifest, getenv func(string) string) []string {
	allowed := map[string]bool{}
	for _, name := range settings.Environment {
		allowed[name] = true
	}
	names := append([]string(nil), settings.Environment...)
	for _, name := range manifest.Environment {
		if allowed[name] && !contains(names, name) {
			names = append(names, name)
		}
	}
	...
```

`names` starts with ALL settings.Environment entries. The loop adds manifest names that are in allowed AND not already in names. Since every element of settings.Environment is in names, and manifest names must be in allowed (=settings.Environment) to be added... any manifest name added would have to be in settings.Environment but not in names — impossible since names contains all of settings.Environment exactly once (assuming config has no duplicates; validated? smoke.environment validation at :503 checks name validity; duplicates maybe not checked). So the loop is dead code unless settings.Environment contains duplicate names AND... no: if "PATH" appears twice in settings.Environment, names has it twice; manifest PATH would be skipped by !contains. Still dead.

So effectively: **env forwarded = settings.Environment ∩ set-in-process-env**. manifest.Environment is completely inert. The context pack's claim ("name set = settings.Environment ∩ manifest.Environment") is wrong about the code.

Now what's the intended contract? Check TRD §18.9.2: "bounded env forwarding". Let me check the workspace TRD text to see if the manifest's environment list is supposed to gate forwarding. Also check the test TestDefaultSmokeEnvironmentPreservesInterpreterPath — does it involve manifest.Environment?

Let me read the test and TRD section.

